{"name":"Grape Soda","hex":"#ae94a6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grape","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, round, smooth-skinned edible fruit, usually purple, red, or green, that grows in bunches on female vines of most species of genus Vitis and the self-fertile plants of species Vitis vinifera.","Any woody vine of genus Vitis that bears clusters of grapes; a grapevine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing grapes or having a grape flavor.","Of a dark purplish red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grape"},{"term":"soda","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Sodium bicarbonate.","Sodium carbonate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/soda"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grape drink","blocks":[{"text":"Grape drinks are sweetened drinks with a grape flavor and a deep purple color. They may be carbonated or not."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grape_drink","wikidata":"Q5597006"},{"title":"Grape","blocks":[{"text":"A grape is a fruit, botanically a berry, of the deciduous woody vines of the flowering plant genus Vitis. Grapes are a non-climacteric type of fruit, generally occurring in clusters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grape","wikidata":"Q10978"},{"title":"Soft drink","blocks":[{"text":"A soft drink is a class of beverage containing no alcohol, usually carbonated, and typically including added sweetener. Flavors can be natural, artificial or a mixture of the two. The sweetener may be a sugar, high-fructose corn syrup, fruit juice, a sugar substitute, or some combination of these. Soft drinks may also contain caffeine, colorings, preservatives and other ingredients. Soft drinks are called \"soft\" in contrast with \"hard\" alcoholic drinks and non-alcoholic drinks. Small amounts of alcohol may be present in a soft drink, but the alcohol content must be less than 0.5% of the total volume of the drink (ABV) in many countries and localities if the drink is to not be considered alcoholic. Examples of soft drinks include lemon-lime drinks, orange soda, cola, grape soda, cream soda, ginger ale and root beer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Tumbler_of_cola_with_ice.jpg/330px-Tumbler_of_cola_with_ice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_drink","wikidata":"Q147538"},{"title":"Shades of violet","blocks":[{"text":"Violet is a color term derived from the flower of the same name. There are numerous variations of the color violet, a sampling of which are shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Color_icon_violet_v3.svg/330px-Color_icon_violet_v3.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_violet","wikidata":"Q17118741"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Grape_Buds.jpg/500px-Grape_Buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Grape_Buds.jpg/1280px-Grape_Buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Grape_Buds.jpg/500px-Grape_Buds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grape flower buds during flowering period.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrape_Buds.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/ConcordGrapes.jpg/500px-ConcordGrapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common